body: "**Version:** 2026.10.23. **Scope:** core runCalendar / CalendarResult, also visible through optional calendar presentation. Medium context-completeness UX. No stored data loss claimed.\n\nRun through npx -y tsx repro.mts in a fresh scratch SDK workspace; no calendar package is needed:\n\n~~~ts\nimport { PmClient, runRemind, runCalendar } from '@unbrained/pm-cli';\nconst c = new PmClient({ cwd: process.cwd(), author: 'codex-agent' });\nawait c.init(undefined, { defaults: true, agentGuidance: 'skip' });\nconst g = { path: process.cwd() + '/.agents/pm', author: 'codex-agent' };\nfor (let n = 1; n <= 3; n++) {\n  await runRemind('Reminder ' + n, { at: '+1d' }, g);\n}\nconst limited = await runCalendar({ view: 'agenda', from: 'now',\n  to: '+7d', limit: '2' }, g);\nconst all = await runCalendar({ view: 'agenda', from: 'now', to: '+7d' }, g);\nconsole.log(limited.summary.events, all.summary.events, Object.keys(limited));\n~~~\n\n**Observed:** **2 versus 3**. Limited keys: view, output_default, now, anchor, range, filters, summary, events, days. Summary counts the returned two reminders; filters.limit='2' is the sole limit disclosure. No matching total, omitted count, has_more, omission receipt, continuation or warning. An exactly-full two-row response cannot distinguish two matches from three. CalendarResult types likewise have no completeness coordinate.\n\nThe larger tracker returned two scheduling rows while omitting 30 deadlines and two additional scheduling rows, **34 matches** overall. This reproduces through the core SDK without any fleet package.\n\n**Expected:** expose returned-versus-total scope and has_more/omitted_count in the core result; supply bounded continuation or a concrete recovery with consistency limits. Post-limit summaries may remain, but label their scope. This is not a request for an unbounded default.\n\n**Measured cost:** tiny independent reproduction: compact limited result **646.75 tokens**, unbounded reread **866.5**, total **1,513.25** over two calls with duplicated rows. Large-tracker CLI: limited **948.5 tokens**, unbounded **12,245.75**, total **13,194.25**. No bounded page-2 operation requests only omitted rows. Full due-work recovery therefore exceeds 2,000 tokens in the measured fallback. Rows are also repeated in events/day buckets; no separate duplication draft is proposed.\n\n**Duplicate searches**, same all-state limit-20 command:\n\n- \"calendar\" \"truncation\"\n- \"calendar\" \"limit\"\n- \"calendar\" \"has_more\"\n- \"calendar\" \"omission\"\n- \"agenda\" \"pagination\"\n- agenda summary limit\n\n#595 was read: list envelope stability. #1554 covers activity continuation, whose result already discloses omissions; this calendar result does not. #1401 concerns context budget accounting. No matching core-calendar completeness report found.\n\n\n\n---\nFound by an agent-UX probe of 2026.10.23 (agent seat and extension-author seat) and re-verified by the maintainer orchestrator against the globally installed 2026.10.23 before filing."
